==In the manga==
[[File:Leonardo Adventures.png|thumb|180px|A male Pokémon Breeder in Pokémon Adventures]]
===Pokémon Adventures===
{{adv|Gold}}, although never officially called breeder, specializes in hatching Pokémon in the [[Pokémon Adventures]] manga. Other characters who can be called "breeders" in this manga are the [[Day-Care Couple]].

====History====
====={{MangaArc|Emerald}}=====
In ''[[PS309|Moving Past Milotic]]'', {{adv|Emerald}} has a [[Double Battle]] at the [[Battle Pike]], going up against virtual male and female Pokémon Breeders who use {{p|Fearow}} and {{p|Raichu}}. They are shown again in a flashback in ''[[PS314|A Sketchy Smattering of Smeargle]]''.

In ''[[PS319|Verily Vanquishing Vileplume I]]'', a female Pokémon Breeder is one of the Trainers that participate in the [[Battle Dome]] challenge. She is pushed aside when {{adv|Emerald}} tries to squeeze in to sit with the challengers.

====={{MangaArc|HeartGold & SoulSilver}}=====
A male Pokémon Breeder made a brief cameo with his {{p|Weavile}} in ''[[PS452|All About Arceus I]]''.

====={{MangaArc|Diamond & Pearl}}=====
In ''[[PS361|Bombastic Bibarel & Heroic Hippopotas]]'', a female Pokémon Breeder appears at the [[Seven Stars Restaurant]].

In ''[[PS391|Luring in a Lickilicky]]'', a female Pokémon Breeder appears during the [[Pokétch]] presentation taking place in [[Jubilife City]].

====={{MangaArc|Platinum}}=====
A Pokémon Breeder was seen in ''[[PS418|Deprogramming Porygon-Z]]'', entering the {{gdis|Battle Frontier|IV}} after [[Palmer]] had his assistants open the gates. In the same chapter, a female Pokémon Breeder was seen waiting in line for the [[Battle Castle]].

In ''[[PS422|Interrupting Ivysaur]]'', a male Pokémon Breeder named '''Leonardo''' (Japanese: '''レオナルド''') is {{adv|Platinum}}'s opponent in the [[Battle Arcade]]. She manages to defeat him with her {{TP|Platinum|Rapidash}} when the panel lands on the sunny panel.

====={{MangaArc|Black & White}}=====
A male Pokémon Breeder was seen in a commercial for the [[Xtransceiver]] in ''[[PS465|Lights, Camera...Action!]]''.

A male Pokémon Breeder with a {{p|Cottonee}} was seen in ''[[PS466|An Odd Speech]]'', listening to [[Ghetsis]]'s speech in [[Accumula Town]].

A female Pokémon Breeder with a {{p|Swanna}} was seen socializing with a group of other Trainers in ''[[PS486|Unraveling Mysteries]]''.

A male Pokémon Breeder with a {{p|Lampent}} appeared in ''[[PS511|Dream a Little Dream]]'' amongst the Trainers entering {{OBP|Victory Road|Black and White}}.

===={{MangaArc|X & Y}}====
In ''[[PS592|Zygarde Agitated]]'', Pokémon Breeders were shown tending {{p|Skiddo}} in [[Baa de Mer Ranch]].

===={{MangaArc|Sun, Moon, Ultra Sun & Ultra Moon}}====
In ''[[PASM36|Regeneration!! The Power of the Sun and the Moon!]]'', a male Pokémon Breeder was one of the people blaming {{tc|Team Skull Grunt}}s for the [[Ultra Beast]]s in [[Alola]] in [[Plumeria]]'s flashback.

